course: dictionary
lesson: 5941
title: Place names with stories
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Massachusetts is a proper noun. It is the special name of one place, so it starts with a capital letter, like Boston and Georgia. Proper nouns name people, places and things that are one of a kind.
explain: «In the 1600s and 1700s English settlers founded thirteen colonies on America's east coast, from Massachusetts to Georgia.» The words «from» and «to» are clues. They show that Massachusetts and Georgia are two places at the two ends of a line, so Massachusetts must be a place on that coast.
explain: Massachusetts is a state, which is a part of a country, here in the USA. Its capital and biggest city is Boston. When you meet a place name you do not know, look for clues about where it is, what it is part of, and what happened there.
fact: Massachusetts is a state in the north-east of the USA.
fact: Massachusetts is in the region called New England.
fact: Boston is the capital and biggest city of Massachusetts.
fact: The Massachusett were a Native American people of the area, and the state is named after them.
fact: In history, the Pilgrims landed at Plymouth, Massachusetts, in 1620 on the Mayflower.
exercise: «In the 1600s and 1700s English settlers founded thirteen colonies on America's east coast, from Massachusetts to Georgia.» Where was Massachusetts? | In the middle of the Pacific Ocean | *On America's east coast | In Africa | Far to the west of California
exercise: «The Pilgrims landed at Plymouth, Massachusetts, in 1620.» What is Massachusetts in this sentence? | A kind of food | A ship | *A place, a state in America | A king
exercise: What is the capital and biggest city of Massachusetts? | *Boston | Plymouth | New York | Georgia
test: Massachusetts is part of which region of the USA? | The Deep South | The Great Plains | The Rocky Mountains | *New England
test: The name Massachusetts is often explained as «near the great hill». Which people is the state named after? | The Pilgrims | *The Massachusett | The Mayflower crew | The English settlers
exam: In «from Massachusetts to Georgia», what do the words «from» and «to» tell you? | *Two places at opposite ends of the same coast | Two ships that sailed in 1620 | Two words that mean the same thing | Two foods that were eaten at the first feast
